  <h2>Read one complete visitor route</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Cedar Museum walking directions</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">Leave Cedar Station through the Main Street exit. Turn right and walk along Main Street for two blocks. At the second traffic light, turn left onto Pine Avenue. Go past the public library. Cross Pine Avenue at the marked crosswalk when the signal allows. The museum is on your right, next to the Bluebird Café and across from the park. If you reach Harbor Hospital, you have gone one block too far.</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You followed the exit, turn point, passed landmark, destination relationships, and too-far check in order.">
    <h3>Reading check: use only the visitor route</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the Main Street exit" data-hint="The first sentence names the station exit." data-fix="The route begins through the Main Street exit."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which station exit establishes the start?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the Main Street exit">the Main Street exit</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the Pine Avenue exit">the Pine Avenue exit</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the park exit">the park exit</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="at the second traffic light" data-hint="The route states an ordinal turn point after two blocks." data-fix="The traveler turns left at the second traffic light."><p class="quiz-question">2. Where does the traveler turn left onto Pine Avenue?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="at the second traffic light">at the second traffic light</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="at the public library">at the public library</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="at Harbor Hospital">at Harbor Hospital</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="It is on the right, next to the café, and across from the park." data-hint="The destination sentence gives one side and two relationships." data-fix="The museum is on the right, next to the café, and across from the park."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which description combines all three destination clues?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It is on the right, next to the café, and across from the park.">It is on the right, next to the café, and across from the park.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It is on the left, behind the café, and inside the park.">It is on the left, behind the café, and inside the park.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It is at the station, between the library and hospital.">It is at the station, between the library and hospital.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The traveler has passed the museum by one block." data-hint="Harbor Hospital is explicitly introduced as the too-far landmark." data-fix="Reaching Harbor Hospital means the traveler has passed the museum by one block."><p class="quiz-question">4. What does reaching Harbor Hospital mean in this route?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The traveler has passed the museum by one block.">The traveler has passed the museum by one block.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The traveler has reached the museum entrance.">The traveler has reached the museum entrance.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The traveler should begin at the hospital.">The traveler should begin at the hospital.</button></div></div>
    </div>
