  <h2>Notice and repair three route errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="to" data-hint="Turn left is a complete direction chunk with no to." data-fix="Turn left at the bank." data-why="Use turn left or turn right directly; do not insert to before the side." data-success-message="Correct. Turn left is complete without to.">
    <h3>Drill 6: remove the extra direction word</h3><p>The turn happens at the bank: <span class="ex">Turn to left at the bank.</span> Tap the unnecessary word.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="turn">Turn</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="to">to</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="left">left</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="bank">at the bank</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="passed" data-hint="After go, use the direction word past, not the past-tense verb passed." data-fix="Go past the public library." data-why="Go past means continue beyond a landmark; passed is the past-tense verb in We passed the library." data-success-message="Correct. The movement chunk is go past the library.">
    <h3>Drill 7: choose the direction word</h3><p>The traveler must continue beyond the library: <span class="ex">Go passed the public library.</span> Tap the form that belongs to a past-tense sentence instead.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="go">Go</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="passed">passed</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="library">the public library</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="across" data-hint="The location relationship requires the complete chunk across from." data-fix="The museum is across from the park." data-why="Across from locates two places on opposite sides; cross the park would describe movement through it." data-success-message="Correct. The opposite-side relationship is across from.">
    <h3>Drill 8: complete the location relationship</h3><p>The museum and park face each other on opposite sides: <span class="ex">The museum is across the park.</span> Tap the incomplete relationship.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="museum">The museum</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="across">across</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="park">the park</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Oral transforms: preserve route meaning</h3>
    <p>Say each complete message before revealing it. Follow the exact communication need.</p>
